#User Stories:
US01: As a customer support representative, I want the Email Router system to connect to designated email services and retrieve incoming messages in real-time so that I can focus on addressing complex customer inquiries efficiently.
US02: As a subject matter expert (SME), I want the Email Router system to automatically categorize incoming emails based on content analysis and route complex inquiries to me so that I can provide specialized responses without being overwhelmed by routine inquiries.
US03: As an IT administrator, I want the Email Router system to provide a dashboard displaying performance metrics, response times, and accuracy so that I can monitor system performance and make necessary adjustments to optimize efficiency.
US04: As a user, I want the Email Router system to generate draft responses for routine inquiries using the Response Generation Engine so that I can review and approve them before dispatch, ensuring accurate and consistent messaging.
US05: As a user, I want the Email Router system to allow manual intervention to override automated processes when necessary so that I can ensure that critical communications receive appropriate attention and handling.
As a Customer Support Representative, I want the Email Router system to automatically categorize incoming messages so that I can focus on handling complex customer inquiries efficiently.
As an IT Administrator, I want the Email Router system to provide a dashboard displaying performance metrics so that I can monitor system performance and make necessary adjustments.
As a Subject Matter Expert (SME), I want the Email Router system to forward only relevant, complex inquiries to me so that I can provide specialized expertise where needed.
As a User, I want the Email Router system to process and classify incoming emails within 5 seconds of receipt so that I can respond to urgent messages promptly.
As a Compliance Officer, I want the Email Router system to comply with GDPR, CCPA, and other data protection regulations so that sensitive information is handled appropriately.

# Product Features:
Feature Name: Email Routing and Categorization
Description: This feature focuses on the core functionality of the Email Router system to connect to designated email services, retrieve incoming messages in real-time, automatically categorize emails based on content analysis, and route complex inquiries to the appropriate recipients.
Key Functionality:
- Connect to designated email services and retrieve incoming messages in real-time
- Automatically categorize incoming emails based on content analysis
- Route complex inquiries to the designated Subject Matter Experts (SMEs)
User Benefit: Users can efficiently handle customer inquiries by focusing on complex issues while routine inquiries are automatically categorized and routed appropriately.
User Stories: [US01, US02, US05]


Feature Name: Performance Monitoring Dashboard
Description: This feature provides IT administrators with a dashboard displaying performance metrics, response times, and accuracy of the Email Router system, enabling them to monitor system performance and make necessary adjustments for optimization.
Key Functionality:
- Display performance metrics, response times, and accuracy on a dashboard
- Monitor system performance and make necessary adjustments
User Benefit: IT administrators can track system performance in real-time, identify areas for improvement, and optimize the efficiency of the Email Router system.
User Stories: [US03]


Feature Name: Automated Response Generation
Description: This feature enables the Email Router system to generate draft responses for routine inquiries using the Response Generation Engine, allowing users to review and approve them before dispatch for accurate and consistent messaging.
Key Functionality:
- Generate draft responses for routine inquiries using the Response Generation Engine
- Allow users to review and approve generated responses before dispatch
User Benefit: Users can save time by leveraging automated responses for routine inquiries while ensuring that the messaging is accurate and consistent.
User Stories: [US04]


Feature Name: Manual Intervention Override
Description: This feature allows users to manually intervene and override automated processes when necessary, ensuring that critical communications receive appropriate attention and handling as per user discretion.
Key Functionality:
- Allow manual intervention to override automated processes
- Ensure critical communications receive appropriate attention and handling
User Benefit: Users have control over the handling of critical communications, ensuring that important messages are addressed promptly and accurately.
User Stories: [US05]



